source('S06','Destinul Tezaurului României — publisher sample','Ilie Schipor','2021','Romanian / Russian','Book / document facsimile','16-page nonconsecutive preview inspected','https://oscarprint.ro/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/schw.pdf','Printed pp. 9–10, 30–31, 51–53, 64–65, 91–92, 105–106, 129–131','Includes the opening archival document and facsimiles: Bark to Alekseev, 28 October 1916, concerning the evacuation proposal.','Only a sample. It does not contain the decisive 1924 report, document 121. Citation given for document 1: RGVIA, f. 2003, op. 1, d. 1474, l. 221 recto/verso; original archive not visited.','Schipor archival reconstruction')
source('S07','Tezaurul BNR între Cazaciocul dezinformării și „Răsucita” româno-rusă (I)','Ilie Schipor interview / AFnews','2024-05-18','Romanian','Interview / research account','Written article read; embedded video not watched','https://afnews.ro/2024/05/18/prof-col-ilie-schipor-tezaurul-bancii-nationale-a-romaniei-intre-cazaciocul-dezinformarii-si-rasucita-romano-rusa-i/','Discussion comparing the 16 February 1917 inventory with the 23 May 1921 RGAE report','Schipor explicitly argues that the gold remained intact through May 1921, based on a denomination-by-denomination comparison.','The original May 1921 inventory and full comparison have not been independently audited. This is the researcher’s claim, not our own verified gram-level reconciliation.','Schipor archival reconstruction')
