source('S14','Treasury explains treatment of Soviet gold and Swedish mint stamps','Assistant Secretary of the Treasury S. P. Gilbert Jr. to Assistant Secretary of State Fred M. Dearing','1921-03-25','English','Contemporary financial record','Full published document read','https://history.state.gov/historicaldocuments/frus1921v02/d724','FRUS 1921, vol. II, doc. 724; file 861.51/1002','Explains the distinction between gold suspected of Soviet origin and gold bearing the official stamp of a friendly country’s mint, including Sweden.','Documents a generic route and administrative rules. It does not identify a Romanian consignment.','US diplomatic records')
