source('S16','The S.S. Carmania gold shipment rejected at New York','S. P. Gilbert Jr. to the Secretary of State','1921-08-11','English','Contemporary financial record','Full published document read','https://history.state.gov/historicaldocuments/frus1921v02/d732','FRUS 1921, vol. II, doc. 732; file 861.51/1257','Records 7,500 imperial gold roubles consigned by the Bank of England to J. P. Morgan & Co.; the New York Assay Office rejected the tender on 10 August.','No Romanian provenance is stated. This is a negative control against turning every Soviet gold shipment into “the Romanian treasure.”','US diplomatic records')
source('S17','Romanian memorandum alleging gold reaching the United States','Romanian Legation to the US Department of State','1921-08-15','English','Contemporary diplomatic allegation','Full published memorandum read','https://history.state.gov/historicaldocuments/frus1921v02/d733','FRUS 1921, vol. II, doc. 733; file 871.51/251','Romania alleged that part of the gold reaching the US was its 1916 deposit being used for Soviet payments abroad.','The memorandum names no ship, bank, weight, assay lot or informant. Authentic evidence of an allegation, not authentication of a shipment.','Romanian diplomatic allegation')
