source('S31','Rușii au găsit, în propriile arhive, documente despre Tezaurul României (I)','Ilie Schipor; Cetatea Cavalerilor article reprinted by ActiveNews','2024-03-15','Romanian','Research article / reconstructed table','Written article and inventory-table image inspected','https://www.activenews.ro/cultura-istorie/Colonel-Dr.-Ilie-Schipor-RUSII-AU-GASIT-IN-PROPRIILE-ARHIVE-DOCUMENTE-DESPRE-TEZAURUL-ROMANIEI-I-Ce-valoare-avea-si-ce-continea-TABEL-188165','Table headed “Numărul de: lăzi / saci”; discussion of Mosyakin’s 2021 volumes','Reconstructs the first shipment by denomination: German marks 45.56%, Austrian crowns 29.31%, Romanian caroli 0.34% of stated BNR value.','An author’s modern table, not the original ledger. Values and case rows reconcile; its Austrian row says 4,397 bags, versus 4,387 in the BNR annex photograph and transcription (S41–S42). The latter reconciles the printed 13,823 total. Host commentary is not endorsed.','Schipor archival reconstruction')
source('S32','Золото Российской империи и большевики. 1917–1922 гг.','Aleksandr G. Mosyakin; Mezhdunarodnye otnosheniya','2021','Russian','Book / facsimile collection','Publisher record and search excerpts; full volumes not read','https://imobook.ru/book/istoriya-istoricheskie-nauki/Zoloto-Rossijskoj-imperii-i-bolsheviki','Three volumes; ISBN 978-5-7133-1649-5; publisher advertises 742 documents','Potential independent access path to RGAE facsimiles cited in Schipor’s later comparison.','Publisher’s broad political framing is not a finding. Preview download timed out; exact Romanian entries and shelfmarks require the volumes.','Mosyakin collection lead')
